markdown <<MARKDOWN
## Modify: Pattern Gallery

Next you will choose a pattern from the gallery. Each one was written by a different author, and your job is to make it your own.

1. Run it as-is first.
2. Change one thing at a time: the count, the spacing, the color, the shape, the size.
3. Add a second loop that adds something new to the scene.
4. Update the comment at the top: name the author and say what you changed.


---

> **Credit it like this**
>
> Before:
> ```python
> # City at Night — original by Ms. Rivera
> ```
>
> After:
> ```python
> # City at Night — original by Ms. Rivera. Changed window count and color; added a third row. Modified by <your name>
> ```
>
> Who it came from + what you changed. A pattern with no comment does not pass, even if it looks great.
MARKDOWN
